---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';
import { PAID_PLUGINS, PLUGIN_NAMES, PLUGIN_PAGES, PRICES, PRICE_LINE, usd } from '../data/pricing';

const open = '(to be decided)';
---

<Base title="Pricing" description={`${SITE.displayName}: the element and snippets are free; the plugins are ${PRICE_LINE} per domain.`}>
  <p class="eyebrow">Project</p>
  <h1>Pricing</h1>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      <span class="tag ok">Free</span> The <code>&lt;{SITE.tagName}&gt;</code> element, every paste-in snippet, the iframe embed, the framework
      examples and the hosting tools cost nothing, for any site, including businesses and online stores (<a href="/licence/#free">Apache-2.0</a>).
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="tag amber">Paid</span> The plugins cost the same for every site, commercial or not. Each licence is for one plugin on one
      domain.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="grid plans">
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Yearly</h3>
      <p class="price">{usd(PRICES.yearly)}<span> / year</span></p>
      <p>Per plugin, per domain. Renews every year until you cancel; after cancelling, it works until the end of the year you paid for.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Lifetime</h3>
      <p class="price">{usd(PRICES.lifetime)}<span> once</span></p>
      <p>Per plugin, per domain. One payment, no end date.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="prose">
    <p>Prices are in US dollars. Payment is by Stripe Checkout; we never see your card details.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="data">
      <thead><tr><th>Plugin</th><th>Yearly</th><th>Lifetime</th><th></th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          PAID_PLUGINS.map((p) => (
            <tr id={p}>
              <td><a href={PLUGIN_PAGES[p].replace('#licence', '')}>{PLUGIN_NAMES[p]}</a></td>
              <td>{usd(PRICES.yearly)}</td>
              <td>{usd(PRICES.lifetime)}</td>
              <td><a class="btn" href={`/buy/?plugin=${p}`}>Buy</a></td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <div class="prose faq">
    <h2 id="covered">What one licence covers</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>The domain you name at checkout, and the same domain with <code>www.</code>.</li>
      <li>One staging subdomain of it that you name, such as <code>staging.example.com</code>. You can change it three times in any 365 days.</li>
      <li>For Shopify, Wix, Framer and HubSpot: your site’s address on the platform, such as <code>your-store.myshopify.com</code>, if you enter it at checkout.</li>
      <li>Local development, always and without a key: <code>localhost</code>, <code>127.0.0.1</code>, and names ending in <code>.local</code> or <code>.test</code>.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Domains are compared after converting international names to their ASCII (punycode) form, so <code>bücher.example</code> and
      <code>xn--bcher-kva.example</code> are the same licence. A licence can’t be for a shared address such as <code>github.io</code> or
      <code>co.uk</code>, only for a domain under it.
    </p>

    <h2 id="faq">Questions</h2>

    <h3 id="which">Do I need a plugin at all?</h3>
    <p>
      No. Every platform with a paid plugin can also use the free <a href="/platforms/html/">HTML snippet</a> (Shopify in a Custom Liquid
      section, WordPress in a Custom HTML block, React and Vue with the element directly). The plugins add editor settings and platform
      features, such as the Shopify block reading a product’s 3D media and the WordPress Media Library.
    </p>

    <h3 id="two-plugins">I use WordPress and Shopify on the same domain.</h3>
    <p>That is two licences: one per plugin. The Elementor widget is part of the WordPress plugin, so WordPress with Elementor is one.</p>

    <h3 id="moving">Can I move a licence to another domain?</h3>
    <p>
      Yes, twice in any 365 days, from <a href="/licence/manage/">Manage a licence</a>. You need the key and the email address you bought
      it with; we email a link to confirm. The old domain stops being covered when you confirm.
    </p>

    <h3 id="staging">What about staging and preview sites?</h3>
    <p>
      One staging subdomain of your domain is included. Platform editors (the Shopify theme editor, the Wix Editor, the Framer canvas, the
      HubSpot page editor) never show the badge. Preview deployments on other hosts, such as <code>*.vercel.app</code>, are not covered.
    </p>

    <h3 id="multisite">WordPress multisite?</h3>
    <p>
      Each site is checked against its own domain. Sites in sub-directories of one domain share that domain’s licence. Sites on their own
      domains or subdomains need their own licence each (a subdomain can also be the licence’s staging subdomain).
    </p>

    <h3 id="agencies">I’m an agency building sites for clients.</h3>
    <p>
      Buy one licence per client domain, with your email or the client’s. You can install and configure it on the client’s site. Agency
      or bulk pricing: {open}.
    </p>

    <h3 id="unlicensed">What happens without a licence, or when it ends?</h3>
    <p>
      The plugin keeps working. Each model shows a small “Unlicensed” link in its corner, and the WordPress plugin shows administrators a
      notice. Nothing is blocked or removed. If our licence server is unreachable, nothing changes for 30 days after the last successful
      check.
    </p>

    <h3 id="privacy">Does the licence check track visitors?</h3>
    <p>
      No. WordPress checks from your server. The other plugins make one cached request per page that sends the key and the plugin name,
      with no cookies and no page address. See <a href="/licence/#checks">licence checks</a>.
    </p>

    <h3 id="refunds">Refunds</h3>
    <p>Refund policy: {open}. A full refund ends the licence.</p>

    <h3 id="tax">VAT and sales tax</h3>
    <p>
      Prices are shown without tax. Whether VAT, GST or sales tax is added at checkout, and for which countries: {open}. Stripe sends a
      receipt for every payment.
    </p>

    <h3 id="renewal">Will I be reminded before a yearly licence renews?</h3>
    <p>Renewal reminders: {open}. You can cancel any time from <a href="/licence/manage/">Manage a licence</a> (billing portal).</p>

    <h3 id="lost-key">I lost my key.</h3>
    <p><a href="/licence/manage/#resend">Have it emailed again</a> to the address you bought it with.</p>

    <h2 id="licence-keys">Where to enter your key</h2>
    <ul>
      {PAID_PLUGINS.map((p) => <li><a href={PLUGIN_PAGES[p]}>{PLUGIN_NAMES[p]}</a></li>)}
    </ul>
    <p>Questions not answered here: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.licensingEmail}`}>{SITE.licensingEmail}</a>.</p>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .plans {
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
  }
  .price {
    font-size: 2rem;
    color: var(--text) !important;
    margin: 0.25rem 0 0.5rem !important;
  }
  .price span {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--text-dim);
  }
  .faq h3 {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }
</style>
